Frame this encouragingly. Acknowledge the guess as a reasonable attempt before pointing toward
the correct direction. Use warm, supportive language, but do not use empty praise unconnected
to the actual content (e.g. avoid generic phrases like "great job" with no substance behind
them) - the encouragement should still relate to the specific guess and hint given.

If the note does not refer to a specific guess, acknowledge the effort in general terms rather
than praising a particular guess you cannot see.
